- duplicatePlantCodeRejected: register P-1 in Q1, register P-1 in Q2 → 409 （同一植株不得转到另一活跃样方）.
- idempotentReplay: register with req-1; again same params → same id, count 1; same requestId different nursery → 409.
- reviewChainAndDeathRules: register; review ALIVE; review PENDING; review DEAD; chain size 3; then review ALIVE → 409; review DEAD again with new requestId → ok (status stays DEAD).
- deathReleasesCapacity: 12 plants, kill 1, register new → ok; active stays 12; then another → 409.
- reviewIdempotency: review req-x ALIVE; replay same → same review id, chain size 1; same requestId different result → 409.
- sealRules: quadrat with plants: some ALIVE, one DEAD, one PENDING → seal → 409. Review pending → ALIVE; seal → ok; snapshot counts (alive, dead, pending=0), plantCodes contains dead plant. Transplant into sealed → 409. Review after seal → 409. Re-seal → same snapshot id.
- queryShowsSourceChainAndCounts: after operations, quadratService.findByCode + plantsOf + reviewChain verify nursery, quadrat, chain, counts.

Test 2 ConcurrencyTest:

```java
@SpringBootTest
class ConcurrencyTest {
    // capacity race: 11 active, 2 threads register → exactly one succeeds
    // death vs new transplant: 12 active; thread A review DEAD on P-1, thread B register P-new
    //   outcomes: both succeed (active 12) or B fails (active 11 after death). assert active <= 12, and if both succeeded active == 12
    // seal vs review: quadrat with 1 PENDING plant; thread A review ALIVE, thread B seal
    //   outcome 1: review commits first → seal succeeds, snapshot pendingCount==0, aliveCount==1
    //   outcome 2: seal commits first → seal fails 409 (pending exists), review succeeds
    //   assert: if sealed, snapshot counts match final DB counts
}
```

Use ExecutorService(2), CountDownLatch start, futures with timeout 30s.

For capacity race determinism: 2 threads, one plant each, quadrat has 11 → exactly one 409. Assert success count == 1 and active == 12.

Death vs transplant: 12 active. Thread A: review DEAD P-01. Thread B: register P-13. Both start at latch. After: count active ≤ 12. If B succeeded → active == 12 (11 alive-ish + new). If B failed with capacity → active == 11. Both valid per commit order. Assert no other exception, and final active ≤ 12, and P-01 status DEAD.

Seal vs review: 1 plant PENDING. A: review ALIVE. B: seal. After: if seal succeeded → snapshot pendingCount==0 and aliveCount==1 and plantCodes=[P-1]; subsequent state consistent. If seal failed → exception message contains 待复核， review succeeded, quadrat still OPEN. Exactly one consistent version: assert snapshot count via findByQuadratId ≤ 1.

Also race both seals? unique constraint covers. Maybe add double-seal race: two threads seal same quadrat (all alive) → both return same snapshot id (second replays). Good test of single version. Add it.

