Note fixed clock affects all tests in this class — fine.

transplantedAt serialized as ISO "2026-02-01T08:00:00Z". Jackson Instant serialization: with JavaTimeModule and WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS disabled (Spring Boot default), Instant → "2026-02-01T08:00:00Z". Assert jsonPath transplantedAt == "2026-02-01T08:00:00Z".

Hmm, H2 TIMESTAMP storage: Timestamp.from(instant) stores "2026-02-01 08:00:00" in the DB session timezone; reading back toInstant gives same instant as long as write/read use same JVM default TZ handling — Timestamp stores millis since epoch, so round-trips exactly. Good.

